# C layout (AGENTS.md §4).
#
# Conformance authority: AGENTS.md. clang-format owns WHITESPACE; /.clang-tidy owns NAMING and
# semantics. The two never overlap: clang-tidy has no check that reports a wrong brace position
# or an over-long line, and clang-format cannot see that a parameter is missing its `_`. Asking
# either to do the other's job is how a repository ends up with neither.
#
# The values are carried over from the sibling repositories Outpost.Warzone, where they were
# measured against ~223,000 lines of C++, and Nomad-Commander. Those trees are C++ and this one is
# NC-Boot C23 (Design/13-self-hosting-bootstrap.md §1), so the C++-only options (namespaces,
# access modifiers, constructor initialisers, lambdas, requires-clauses, the VS unit-test macros)
# are gone; every value that applies to C is unchanged.
#
# `Language: Cpp` is correct for C: clang-format formats C with its C++ style. Verified on
# clang-format 22.1.8 against the .c and .h files in this tree.
#
# ── Status: NOT YET GATED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The phase-0 sources predate this file and are not formatted to it (AGENTS.md §8). They are
# converted in one dedicated change, and that change wires `make check-format` into the Linux CI
# job, pinned to clang-format 18.1.3 -- the version ubuntu-24.04 installs, which is the runner
# .github/workflows/ci.yml already uses. The output changes between releases, so if a local run
# disagrees with CI, compare the version line first.
#
# On Windows the clang-format you have is almost certainly NOT 18: Visual Studio 2026 bundles 22
# at VC\Tools\Llvm\<arch>\bin, and 22 breaks a long call argument list in a different place than
# 18 does. The Linux job is the answer that counts.
#
# Keep ColumnLimit and IndentWidth in step with /.editorconfig; if you change one, change the other
# in the same commit or they start lying to each other.
#
# ── What is NOT formatted ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# X-macro tables (*.def, AGENTS.md §2) are column-aligned by hand so that a table reads as a
# table, and clang-format would collapse every column. The format check passes *.c and *.h only.
# A run of hand-aligned rows inside a .c or .h (a static table of encodings, say) is fenced with
# `// clang-format off` / `// clang-format on` and nothing else is.
#
# ── Deliberate choices ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# LineEnding is left at its default (DeriveLF) ON PURPOSE. /.gitattributes pins the working-tree
# line ending of every C file, and deriving per file means the formatter never fights it.
#
# AlignConsecutive{Assignments,Declarations} are OFF: clang-format cannot express "align this
# short run but not that one", and switching them on aligns unrelated statements across whole
# blocks.
#
# ReflowComments is OFF so that the block comments explaining a decision keep the line breaks
# their author chose.

Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Standard: Latest

ColumnLimit: 140
IndentWidth: 2
TabWidth: 2
UseTab: Never
ContinuationIndentWidth: 2

# Allman: every brace on its own line -- functions, structs, enums and control flow alike.
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman

IndentCaseLabels: false

IndentPPDirectives: AfterHash
PPIndentWidth: 3

# Arena* _arena, not Arena *_arena.
PointerAlignment: Left
ReferenceAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false

# Control flow never folds onto one line; an empty body may.
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Empty
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Empty
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: false

SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements

AlignConsecutiveAssignments: None
AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: None
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AlignEscapedNewlines: Left
AlignTrailingComments: true

# Include order is grouped by hand (AGENTS.md §4): a .c includes its own header first, then other
# project headers, then the standard library, and no platform header appears outside the OS layer.
# The own-header-first position is the self-containment check for that header, and the
# include-with-parameters pattern (`#define HMAP_K ...` then `#include "core/hmap.inc"`) makes the
# position of an #include part of its meaning. A formatter reordering these is a correctness risk,
# not a style preference.
SortIncludes: Never
IncludeBlocks: Preserve

BinPackArguments: true
BinPackParameters: true
Cpp11BracedListStyle: true
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: false
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 1
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 1
ReflowComments: false
